2. c4 { White challenges the d5 pawn from the side. } 2... e6 { Black supports d5 and opens the f8 bishop’s diagonal. } 3. Nf3 { White develops while keeping the central tension. } 3... Nf6 { Black develops and adds control of e4. } 4. cxd5 { White chooses to exchange the c-pawn for the d5 pawn. } 4... exd5 { Black recaptures with the e-pawn, producing a new pawn structure. } *

