3. d4 { White offers a central pawn exchange to free the pieces. } 3... cxd4 { Black trades the c-pawn for White’s d-pawn. } 4. Nxd4 { White recaptures with the f3 knight, developing its central influence. } 4... Nf6 { Black develops and attacks e4. } 5. Nc3 { White develops a knight that supports e4. } *

